{"id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-21","title":"lem:2-21","path":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":179,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:2-21","uses":["[[references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-20]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:2-21","line":288,"source":"\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lem:2-21}\n\n\\uses{lem:2-20}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.21}\nFor $r_1<r_2$, there is a smooth $h:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ with $h=1$ on $(-\\infty,r_1]$, $0<h<1$ on $(r_1,r_2)$, and $h=0$ on $[r_2,\\infty)$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch With $f$ from Lemma~\\ref{lem:2-20}, set\n\\[\nh(t)=\\frac{f(r_2-t)}{f(r_2-t)+f(t-r_1)}.\n\\]\nThe denominator is positive and the stated values follow from the support properties of $f$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section> <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a322d3231\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeSmooth%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3A2-20\">↗ lem:2-20</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.21</span></span>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r_1&lt;r_2$\">$r_1&lt;r_2$</span>, there is a smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h:\\mathbb R\\to \\mathbb R$\">$h:\\mathbb R\\to \\mathbb R$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h=1$\">$h=1$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(-\\infty ,r_1]$\">$(-\\infty ,r_1]$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0&lt;h&lt;1$\">$0&lt;h&lt;1$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r_1,r_2)$\">$(r_1,r_2)$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h=0$\">$h=0$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[r_2,\\infty )$\">$[r_2,\\infty )$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch With <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> from Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeSmooth%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3A2-20\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-20\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a322d3230\">3</a>, set </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  h(t)=\\frac{f(r_2-t)}{f(r_2-t)+f(t-r_1)}.  \\]\">\\[  h(t)=\\frac{f(r_2-t)}{f(r_2-t)+f(t-r_1)}.  \\]</span></p><p> The denominator is positive and the stated values follow from the support properties of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-20","next":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:2-10-extra-1","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-20","title":"lem:2-20","label":"lem:2-20"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:2-10-extra-1","title":"def:2-10-extra-1","label":"def:2-10-extra-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-22","title":"lem:2-22","label":"lem:2-22"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-21","title":"lem:2-21","tex":"\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lem:2-21}\n\n\\uses{lem:2-20}\n\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.21}\nFor $r_1<r_2$, there is a smooth $h:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ with $h=1$ on $(-\\infty,r_1]$, $0<h<1$ on $(r_1,r_2)$, and $h=0$ on $[r_2,\\infty)$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch With $f$ from Lemma~\\ref{lem:2-20}, set\n\\[\nh(t)=\\frac{f(r_2-t)}{f(r_2-t)+f(t-r_1)}.\n\\]\nThe denominator is positive and the stated values follow from the support properties of $f$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeSmooth/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:2-20","title":"lem:2-20","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}